                <path
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="2"
                  d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-6 pb-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              <p class="mb-3">
                Yes, but image quality will be lower than a dedicated screen.
                <strong>White or light gray walls</strong> work best.
              </p>
              <p class="mb-3">
                For optimal results, use <strong>projector screen paint</strong>
                (gain 1.0-1.3) on a smooth wall.
              </p>
              <p>
                A proper screen provides better contrast, color accuracy, and viewing
                angles compared to bare walls.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details
            class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden group border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700"
